{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting","id":499845,"title":"Art of Witch Hunting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-01T22:51:57-07:00","id":499845,"title":"Art of Witch Hunting","content":"Mine groups return to our <b>Mage</b> game about Hieromagus, ancient ruins, Archmasters shenningans and Abyss chasing PCs. To make things even more interesting, I concider of using the witch hunters this time - I have a strong subplot of Seers in background and were considering of putting players againts <b>Division Six</b> ( from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/51069-assasin-s-creed-series-as-mage-the-awakening-chronicle\">Abstergo Indrustries faction</a> ) and <b>Malleus Maleficarum</b> ancient hunters group that know more about main plot from Vatican Archives.<br /> <br /> The question of topic is simple - <b>How Sleepers can hunt mages effectively? </b>And I mean without going with Banishers. I really want this to be &quot;mortals threat&quot;, not next Awakened that fight with PCs.<br /> <br /> As I see, problem is bigger than you think - Awakened are very powerfull individuals and cabal of six of them ( mine now PCs group ) is really force to be recon with. Sleepers can make problems of vulgar magic when they see it, but one good spell and whole teams of witch hunters can gone. *pufff*<br /> <br /> <b>So how Sleepers hunt our Awakened, in the end, to not get killed and win the day?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-08-2015, 03:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T23:39:23-07:00","id":499901,"title":"","content":"Honestly, there really isn't anything the <i>Malleus Maleficarum</i> can do to any decently experienced Mage cabal directly. There's a reason that the <i>Witchfinders</i> book provides non-Awakened Mages and recommends against using powerful Awakened as adversaries.<br /> <br /> The only way to level the playing field in a direct confrontation would be to give the Hunters some anti-magic artifact, otherwise they'd be limited to harassing the Mages' families and friends or causing other, political and social, challenges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T23:56:27-07:00","id":499924,"title":"","content":"I am going to pit Witch Hunters post 2e who stumble upon a master. They don't have a supernatural templates ability to resist magic... that Thyrsus is going to just look at you crossly, and you die. <br /> <br /> To answer your quesrion:<br /> Honestly, the only way you can do much is to bring overwhelming firepower and numbers if you are going to do straight combat (and your mages will likely still win). <br /> <br /> Instead, have them go around the mages and use connections to shut them down. Have them call in contacts that have the ability to ruin the mages lives: cut off their water and power, have theither assets seized, etc. Remember that mages are humans and still live amongst sleepers. pull apart their lived and support and then when they are distracted, kill them.<br /> <br /> Or use explosives... lots and lots of explosives. You nwver know. You might get lucky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T01:02:24-07:00","id":499979,"title":"","content":"Assassination. Don't do straight up combat, just pick them off one at a time in rapid succession.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T01:11:11-07:00","id":499986,"title":"","content":"We start our game after PCs resettle in the new reality ( <i>very</i> long story ) so each cabal member is on his own and even do not remeber the rest, for now. Maybe individual members are easier to pick up? If yes, how Sleepers could get them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=499979#post499979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assassination. Don't do straight up combat, just pick them off one at a time in rapid succession.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea on general hunter theme. It could work with <b>Division Six</b>. But I do not see this with <b>Mallus Maleficarum</b>, because of their general Modus Operandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-02-2015, 04:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T01:17:24-07:00","id":499988,"title":"","content":"Take them out in a single strike, don't give them time to respond. Depending on how paranoid they are, drugging them with something that knocks them out before they realize something is up might work. Afterwards though, you'll need to keep them drugged and unable to think clearly. If they can think, they can form an imago, and if they can form an imago, they can probably escape or kill their captures.<br /> <br /> Though vigilant use of Fate magic makes everything a lot harder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T02:17:02-07:00","id":500025,"title":"","content":"Nice point about drugging them on. I assume most Witch Hunters made Tactics and Endoments based on mages loosing focus, so they are have really problem with forming Imago. I assume some Condition is in order? The problem are Life wielding sorceres, but mine PCs do not have those, most of the group. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I must see <b>Witch Finders</b> book if <i>Divison Six </i>or <i>Mallus</i> do not have some tricks that could be used on PCs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-02-2015, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T08:31:29-07:00","id":500411,"title":"","content":"I imagine it's going to be a more clear thing in Second Edition, when mages can hold fewer spells at once, it takes longer to cast even when you Reach for it, there are more complications to account for and the risks of Paradox are greater. I would say that a mage who goes into heavily kitted out for scenarios other than fighting are going to be troubled if a fight should break out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T09:11:43-07:00","id":500483,"title":"","content":"oh, I am not saying they cannot do it even in 1e. But if the mage knows you are coming, you are screwed. and once you reveal yourself, they can start mounting a defense. <br /> <br /> I mentioned this in the other cross-over thread: mages grow in power the longer thry have time to engage. They start just above a baseline human, but the longer they have time to consider a reaponse, the more god-like they can become. That is why you need to overwhelm them in a fight with numbers and/or firepower, since it keeps them distracted and on the defensive, because if you give them any time to think and respond, thry will either hit back hard or get away.<br /> <br /> Yes, they are still human and cannot prepare for everything. But like humanity, given enough time, and they can get up to some ridiculous stuff. They just have the means to do so very efficiently. So an assassination when they have no idea you are coming is the best way to take them out as a Hunter. snipe them, poison them, car bomb, whatever. But hope you get them on the first try.<br /> <br /> And if they are supposed to antagonist for a mage chronicle, the assassination method doesn't work, cause then your players will be pissed that you essentially pulled a ST fiat. It is realistic but not any fun. <br /> <br /> Considering Wyrd's characters survived the Abyss to return to an alternate reality while fleeing from an Archmage they pissed off, I was assuming they have some degree of skill and finesse, as well as a hefty bit of brute power, so they aren't going to be an easy Cabal to threaten. I think the better Compacts would be TFV or the Aegis Kai Doru:<br /> - TFV let's you bring the US government down on them, which is enough to make any mages life hell, even if their agents don't quite get it. When the IRS repossessed your home, you are on America's Most Wnted as a Terrorist, and guys in fatigues with laser cannons are after you... you can almost get a Technocrat game going.<br /> - the AKD has both a shared back story (they think they descend from atlantis, but mages stole their power) and magical artifacts that you can simulate as mage Artifacts/Imbued items (or not, to keep the mages guessing) which can let you make things interesting (shit! He has a thaumium sword! I can't hit him with my spells!)<br /> <br /> Also, keep in mind paradox and run with it. Use sleepers to weaken the mages. Have them attack in the mall. I also count standard TFV members as sleepers, since of all conspiracies, they still don't seem to get what is going on and thry rely completely on (advanced) mortal technology. <br /> <br /> Anyway, just my 2 cents from running games with Hunters as antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T10:02:49-07:00","id":500522,"title":"","content":"First of - thanks for ideas. I will answer some to maybe plan better the capturing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=500483#post500483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, they are still human and cannot prepare for everything. But like humanity, given enough time, and they can get up to some ridiculous stuff. They just have the means to do so very efficiently. So an assassination when they have no idea you are coming is the best way to take them out as a Hunter. snipe them, poison them, car bomb, whatever. But hope you get them on the first try.<br /> <br /> And if they are supposed to antagonist for a mage chronicle, the assassination method doesn't work, cause then your players will be pissed that you essentially pulled a ST fiat. It is realistic but not any fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that less martial PCs could be bring to the questioning rather than immediately assassination. I will point it more later, but game start with characters being splited, do not remebering they previous role of quasi-Messihas, with Abyssal Taint now. They are suspecting, but even Conspiracies, I suppose, rather would like to question them first, kill them later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=500483#post500483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- TFV let's you bring the US government down on them, which is enough to make any mages life hell, even if their agents don't quite get it. When the IRS repossessed your home, you are on America's Most Wnted as a Terrorist, and guys in fatigues with laser cannons are after you... you can almost get a Technocrat game going.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most characters are British, and action of game is, generally, in London. I think that TFV would be in this bad idea, but maybe <i>Knights of Saint George</i>, as they are quasi-official Englands witch hunters? Could use <i>Lords Stewards</i> for govemrnt thing, but I think they will be too soft for &quot;we need to capture or kill those reality deviants&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=500483#post500483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- the AKD has both a shared back story (they think they descend from atlantis, but mages stole their power) and magical artifacts that you can simulate as mage Artifacts/Imbued items (or not, to keep the mages guessing) which can let you make things interesting (shit! He has a thaumium sword! I can't hit him with my spells!)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's very interesintg proposition. I posted <i>Divison Six</i> becuase of their unobvious connection to the Seers ( large antagonists of previous season of game ) and they rather drastic Modus Operandi - good on the martial part of the previous cabal and new Bond movies feel for this subplot.<br /> <br /> <i>Malleus Maleficarum</i>, on the other hand, beside being concerned with hunting witches, can be easily connected by the Hieromagus plot - they can easily thinks that PCs are false Messiahs, that are deluded to think are next Jesus. Not without some clues from jelous Guardians of Veil cabal, planning to take out probable problems before they PC will start them. Now Abyssal Taint on PCs only corrects that they can by &quot;Anti-Christs&quot; to the eyes of the Shadow Congregation. I imagine that <i>Malleus</i> presence in UK has risen after new apostolic constitution in 2009 - <i><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anglicanorum_Coetibus\" target=\"_blank\">Anglicanorum Coetibus</a> </i>- that basiclly allow anglicans to become part of Catholic Church.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-02-2015, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T10:35:45-07:00","id":500534,"title":"","content":"Well, there is nothing saying that the Bits don't have their own version of TFV. And they would have a lot more resources (imagine how many camera are in London... who is scrying who now?).<br /> <br /> But the KSGs are a great group to throw at them. If your guys are abyssal tainted, maybe it means they can sense your characters (since they serve abyssal beings). And they aren't going to soft. They view magic as bringing about the end of the world and want to kill off mages (remember:they serve the Abyss!).<br /> <br /> And if the Seers are central, just make Division 6 scarier. And remember, they are US based too, so just like TFV, you would need to make the British version too.<br /> <br /> But yeah, those were just ideas. I really don't know how things are set up in your game, so I am just working from general principles in the lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T12:25:02-07:00","id":500605,"title":"","content":"Use attacks in mall with caution. With certain groups you are going to end up with a few Manifestations in the mall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T12:44:40-07:00","id":500626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korusef</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=500605#post500605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Use attacks in mall with caution. With certain groups you are going to end up with a few Manifestations in the mall.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you mean more fun for the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T17:05:37-07:00","id":500993,"title":"","content":"Your going to have to give them something to give them an edge, because as has been mentioned they can easily be picked apart by potent mages if your not talking about assassination attempts bombs ect you might wanna read about &quot;The lucid&quot; from the unbidden book. (Sleepwalkers with a mages unseen senses that make them hate magic)<br /> <br /> Another option if your definitely trying to avoid supernatural elements is some novel tool that close that gap.<br /> <br /> Call me uninspired but I'm suggesting something like Orbo from &quot;witch hunter robin&quot; an anime about witch hunting police force but suitably different to match the theme of your chronical and not be a blatant rip off :P<br /> <br /> Orbo in that series is a Green fluid, It can be used Defensively and Offensively against &quot;craft users&quot; Defensively it's put into Jewelry (Usually crucifix style amulets) It reacts against magic becoming the target of the spell instead of the person absorbing much of it's potency. In that series it's shown to save the lives of several cast members when they get targeted by &quot;witches&quot; who have abilities like &quot;I make you explode by looking at you/Touching me makes you age to dust&quot; merely knocking out the character and breaking the amulet.<br /> <br /> Offensively they place it into Glass ampoules with a sedative and fire it at witches once it enters the bloodstream the effect is to gradually weaken and then nullify there magics then rendering the &quot;witch&quot; unconscious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4641-pebbles","name":"Pebbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T19:59:42-07:00","id":501250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=500522#post500522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most characters are British, and action of game is, generally, in London. I think that TFV would be in this bad idea, but maybe <i>Knights of Saint George</i>, as they are quasi-official Englands witch hunters? Could use <i>Lords Stewards</i> for govemrnt thing, but I think they will be too soft for &quot;we need to capture or kill those reality deviants&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Always figured that TFV was more &quot;NATO&quot; structured where it's basically the US providing logistics with local countries supporting their own groups. Thus, it would be perfectly acceptable to have TFV personal and/or equipment show up in a game where it's mostly supporting the local government backed conspiracies.<br /> <br /> But outside the US, I would think that TFV really only shows up personally if you've done something to grab their attention (Interfering with US base personal, magical &quot;terrorism&quot;, etc.) so I don't see them active in a London game that much other than perhaps puppet masters or &quot;Allies of my enemy&quot;.<br /> <br /> Still, it gives you a nice excuse to put them in if things really start getting loud and deadly with the local government hunter cells as they start calling in favors to TFV.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T20:13:56-07:00","id":501264,"title":"","content":"<b>Pebbles</b>, thanks for mentionig <b>Witch Hunter Robin</b> - I've seen this series ages ago and it will help in our topic here. Time to return to the <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">STN-J and their Endowments. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Fo those that did not see this series, here is trailer:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7UkaILjPk8M\" data-code=\"7UkaILjPk8M\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/7UkaILjPk8M/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Still, Robin IS a Banisher in the series - and I wanted to omit it as much as possible. There were enough Mage vs Mage conflicts - time to show Sleepers can be denegerous to Awakened still.<br /> <br /> The main idea to steal from <b>WHR</b> is that there are things that can change you as the target for the tiems itself. I think that some Voodoo dolls or other Sympathy Connected items could work in this vein - you target owner of the item, but spell goes on the item on them.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-02-2015, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T20:24:34-07:00","id":501272,"title":"","content":"The main problem is that I clearly do not want to kill PCs mages - mainly to lock down them, hurt yes, but without killing them. Both goups Modus Operand must take in consideration that they need to be put on &quot;trial&quot; ( interigation, in reality ) and they higher ups need to decide what to do with them. Other way we do not have the chronicle, if we kill heroes of the story. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Once again thanks, <b>Pebbles</b>, I will check the &quot;The Lucid&quot;.<br /> <br /> We need weapons that drug, weak or just unfocus characters, <i>not that kill them</i>. Seeing also my players in actions - some Endowmnets for breaking Mage Shield would be also very suitable.<br /> <br /> I will write the Condition for the <i>Unfocused</i> mages that cannot form Imago. I think it will be cool and logical idea to explore in <b>Mage</b> setting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-02-2015, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T21:11:40-07:00","id":501332,"title":"","content":"Mages aren't terribly easy to generalize on. Different Paths mean different common powers. What a Mage expects, predicts, and waits for is important.<br /> <br /> For example, many have wards on their homes, but are many monitoring their cars? Watch their routine, follow them to work, attach a car bomb there or plant an IED on their route. If they go to bars, get one good and drunk, send an attractive team member or prostitute to lure them into an alley, and give them a shotgun serenade.<br /> <br /> The trick when dealing with any and all supernaturals is overwhelming firepower and the element of surprise. They have the advantage in both, almost always, but they're not omniscient or omnipotent. Use that. It's really the only way to win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T02:56:01-07:00","id":501584,"title":"","content":"Can't the MM ressurect people, or at least magically heal them? Why not just go all out? Cut the cabal down in a hail of gunfire and you can heal them while you cart them away to your interogation room. I've used that tactic with inter-mage combat before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T07:46:38-07:00","id":502898,"title":"","content":"Sleepers are also tremendously vulnerable to Acanthus shinanigans - if a witch should keep a weather eye on the future with magic, they'll spot plots and plans comming a week away and start writing a Sleeper's obituary even before they start making a move. The paranoid standard Mastigos is also going to have an edge on Hunters who starts obsessing over them, as they're most likely to spot new sympathetic connections forming when people start spying on their every move, and will eventually take steps against that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1516-solarious","name":"Solarious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T09:39:18-07:00","id":503018,"title":"","content":"I've done a couple things. I have an organization with TF:V that the party keeps running afoul of. They are well equipped and knowledgeable at this point.<br /> <br /> 1) Two hunters side by side with Barrett 50-cal sniper rifles, firing armor piercing, blessed rounds. When they launch an attack like this the worst I've done was knock the mage unconscious. It wouldn't really be fair to auto-kill them like this.<br /> <br /> 2) I've had the Highlander type thing - a black van screeched to a halt in front of the party and the side door opened to have four guys going all out with machine guns.<br /> <br /> 3) The players home is the top floor of the apartment building. It is warded, etc. The group tried to bring down the entire building with C4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2060-cthulusbuttcheeks","name":"CthulusButtCheeks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T11:42:05-07:00","id":503194,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering how helpful it is to a witch hunter to studiously ignore any magical effects...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T23:44:13-07:00","id":508799,"title":"","content":"Here are the new mechanics I work for my <i>real</i> Witch Hunters \u2013 those that fight the Awakened characters. I hope you like them and that I look forward for all your comments. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>New Conditions</b></span><br /> <br /> Key to fighting with witches is to not let her use magic. Character with<b> Unfocused</b> has problem with concentrate enough to cast spells in her mind \u2013 and by this, form any Imago. She could be drugged, mentally shattered by the events on her personal life or any other reason she cannot focus enough. Effect is the same \u2013 witch is powerless without her magic. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Unfocused</b></span><br /> <b>Prequistion: </b>Mage<br /> Your character cannot think clearly and by this cast spells as long as the source of this Condition is not resolved. Until then any action of spellcasting is treated as Failure. If character still insist on this, she can spend Willpower point and roll the Chance Roll \u2013 however, all spells cast in this state are treated as vulgar magic and trigger Paradox Rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Intoxination. Life shattering events, like close ones in real danger or seeing them dead.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution:</b> The source of the Condition leaves your body or mind and she can focus on her spells once more.<br /> <br /> <b>Beat:</b> Your character takes an action that highlight her focus problems with magic. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Witch Hunters Endowments</b></span><br /> <br /> Those new mechanics are templates for the new Endowments. Almost all Conspiracies have variants of this powers as the tech ( like Advanced Armory of TFV ), relics ( like Aegis Kai Doru ) or innate powers ( like Malleus Maleficarum or Lucifuge ), as they are central to hunting witches. If you got cool names for them in Conspiracies, do not hesitate to write them below. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Notice:</b> When text mentions Endowment Merit it means this particular characters support from the Conspiracy- like Benediction, Advanced Armory, Relics and a like ratings. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Sympathy Dummy</b></span><br /> <br /> To make successful hunt and using other Endowments, hunter need to be able to resist witches spell. At least once, so he could take his strike on her. This Endowment is making some item on the hunter taking spells on to itself, instead of the hunter by the Law of Sympathy \u2013 or other magical nonsense like this. Most of the time, magic will do nothing to the Dummy, as it was not the part of Imago for spell.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Willpower - Automatic<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> None<br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics: </b>Sympathy Dummy automatically takes each casted spell on the user, up to number of Endowment Merit\u2019s points in the scene. Each next magic goes straight on the hunter.<br /> <br /> <b>Variants Example:</b> Voodoo Doll ( Relics ), Consecrated Cross ( Benedictions )<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Mage Shield Breaker</b></span><br /> <br /> One of largest problems when facing witches \u2013 beside their using of spells \u2013 is that they are covered in mystical armors, like \u201cthick air\u201d or the luck is always guiding bullets away from it. This Endowment take out this advantage. Using this Endowment needs the direct contact the source of it with the witch ( item in case of tech or relics, hunter himself in case of innate powers ).<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Willpower<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant, Touch<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Resolve + Endowment Merit contested with targets Stamina + Gnosis (if have )<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> Instead of taking of witches mystical armor, the hunter is exposed. He lose the number of Armor points equal to this Endowment Merit for the next scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> Nothing happens<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> Witch lose the advantages from her Mage Armor and cannot invoke any other till the end of scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> As with success, but witch gets also Unfocused Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Modi\ufb01ers</b><br /> +2 Hunter using the Endowment in the ways that simulates breaking the shield with weapon \u2013 like pricing \u201cthick air\u201d around the witch.<br /> <br /> <b>Variants Example:</b> Magic Stealing Rod ( Relics ), Arm of Banisher ( Taumatechnology )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T01:38:43-07:00","id":508820,"title":"","content":"Seeing as how you're using Conditions I'll assume we're talking 2e. First, if spending willpower on Unfocused, they should use their full spellcasting dicepool without the benefits of having spent Willpower. Spending a point of WP for nothing but a chance die is too much. Also, there's no vulgar/covert distinction in 2e, so that isn't really applicable. I'd say it could require 1 reach to cast at all but there's no reason for this one condition to apply both effects (reach requirement <i>and</i> willpower to cast), it should be one or the other.<br /> <br /> As for Mage Shield Breaker, mage shield is no longer a spell, they are attainments. I don't really think that those are something a hunter should be able to just turn off. If you want to pierce through their defenses you just need to use equipment designed to pierce armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T02:49:57-07:00","id":508848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=508820#post508820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing as how you're using Conditions I'll assume we're talking 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Storytelling System Second Edition, not Mage 2ED, as those we do not have, for now. Basiclly, it's for using Mage 1ED with God Machine Rules Update. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=508820#post508820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, if spending willpower on Unfocused, they should use their full spellcasting dicepool without the benefits of having spent Willpower.<br /> <br /> Spending a point of WP for nothing but a chance die is too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would let character roll almost their normal Dice Pools - in 1ED mages rolls Gnosis + Arcanum or Gnosis + Arcanum + Skill for rotes. With Willpower point spent it would be just +3 dice bonus to the roll. The <i>point</i> of Unfocused Condition is to weakening the mage to be almost powerless - she is so distrated, she cannot think clearly, is it drugs in her vains or the emotional burden of personal trauma. You know, scenes like &quot;I cannot bear this!&quot; or totally half-conciese guy, bealy stedning on his feets from sedetives.<br /> <br /> I think that character could use with Willpower point Gnosis <b>OR</b> Arcanum only. I would go with Arcanum, as it's basic knowlegde of the Mystieres used in spell, and also this trait is both in normal casting and in rotes. Character is very much on disadvantage here and hunters have a chance to put her down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=508820#post508820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, there's no vulgar/covert distinction in 2e, so that isn't really applicable. I'd say it could require 1 reach to cast at all but there's no reason for this one condition to apply both effects (reach requirement <i>and</i> willpower to cast), it should be one or the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have your answer for full Mage 2ED rules then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=508820#post508820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Mage Shield Breaker, mage shield is no longer a spell, they are attainments. I don't really think that those are something a hunter should be able to just turn off. If you want to pierce through their defenses you just need to use equipment designed to pierce armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, Armor on character in GMC and 2ED is <b>very</b> powerfull thing. From the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/314-stop-gap-god-machine-mechanics-for-mage\">Stop Gap Rules Patch for Mage</a>, we know that Shields work for Defense or Armors - and could work for both. That means that you easily could have Mysterium librarian with Defence about 7 and Armor about 3 ( Dexterity and Wits on 2, Athletics on 2, two Arcana on 3 ). The Adamantine Arrows could gone up to Defence about 12. <b>Not</b> considering Merits.<br /> <br /> To beat those numbers, Hunters need to be like Specnaz commando guys - and we do know they are mostly not. This is why the Endowments exists - to make Hunters able to take a really powerfull Enemy.<br /> <br /> As to what to do with <b>Mage Shield Breaker</b> - maybe the Endoment nullifues up to Endoment Merits points on the Shield? So starting Conspiracy Hunter can only little weak the Awakened - but Lord-Inquisitor of Mallues could slice through it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T03:27:05-07:00","id":508854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=508848#post508848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Storytelling System Second Edition, not Mage 2ED, as those we do not have, for now. Basiclly, it's for using Mage 1ED with God Machine Rules Update. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It would let character roll almost their normal Dice Pools - in 1ED mages rolls Gnosis + Arcanum or Gnosis + Arcanum + Skill for rotes. With Willpower point spent it would be just +3 dice bonus to the roll. The <i>point</i> of Unfocused Condition is to weakening the mage to be almost powerless - she is so distrated, she cannot think clearly, is it drugs in her vains or the emotional burden of personal trauma. You know, scenes like &quot;I cannot bear this!&quot; or totally half-conciese guy, bealy stedning on his feets from sedetives.<br /> <br /> I think that character could use with Willpower point Gnosis <b>OR</b> Arcanum only. I would go with Arcanum, as it's basic knowlegde of the Mystieres used in spell, and also this trait is both in normal casting and in rotes. Character is very much on disadvantage here and hunters have a chance to put her down.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You have your answer for full Mage 2ED rules then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, Armor on character in GMC and 2ED is <b>very</b> powerfull thing. From the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/314-stop-gap-god-machine-mechanics-for-mage\">Stop Gap Rules Patch for Mage</a>, we know that Shields work for Defense or Armors - and could work for both. That means that you easily could have Mysterium librarian with Defence about 7 and Armor about 3 ( Dexterity and Wits on 2, Athletics on 2, two Arcana on 3 ). The Adamantine Arrows could gone up to Defence about 12. <b>Not</b> considering Merits.<br /> <br /> To beat those numbers, Hunters need to be like Specnaz commando guys - and we do know they are mostly not. This is why the Endowments exists - to make Hunters able to take a really powerfull Enemy.<br /> <br /> As to what to do with <b>Mage Shield Breaker</b> - maybe the Endoment nullifues up to Endoment Merits points on the Shield? So starting Conspiracy Hunter can only little weak the Awakened - but Lord-Inquisitor of Mallues could slice through it?</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm trying to say is that the condition is overpowered as is. If you want to make it so they can't think, just drug them up so they have the Insensate/Drugged Condition/Tilt. Making them unfocused in a way that only hinders casting isn't really a thing imo. You're either drugging them so hard they can't function at all (Insensate/Drugged/Etc.) or you're making them woozy but still functional (requiring willpower or additional reach).<br /> <br /> Mage Shield isn't going to work the same way it does in the stop-gap. IIRC we've been told that there's going to be a weaker constant effect and then a stronger full shield effect requiring mana expenditure. So with it probably requiring resources to use anyways, I'd again suggest using heavier weapons or running them out of mana with a continuous assault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 05-09-2015, 06:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T05:41:47-07:00","id":508871,"title":"","content":"I will quote the <i>Stunned</i> Tilt from <b>God Machines Rules Update</b> for the discussion - I hope it's okay with forum rules, as the material is free on DriveThru.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God Machine Rules Update</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Stunned</b><br /> Your character is dazed and unable to think straight. Maybe her vision blurs. If she\u2019s stunned as a result of a blow to the head, she\u2019s probably got a concussion.<br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> A character with the Stunned Tilt loses her next action, and halves her Defense until she can next act.<br /> <br /> <b>Causing the Tilt:</b> A character can be stunned by any attack that does at least as much damage as her Size in a single hit. Some weapons have a \u201cstun\u201d special ability. These double the weapon modifier only for the purposes of determining whether the attacker inflicts the Stunned Tilt. Attacks against the target\u2019s head (see \u201cSpecified Targets,\u201d p. 203) count the character\u2019s Size as one lower for the purposes of this Tilt. The Storyteller might determine that additional effects cause this Tilt, like being caught in the blast area of an explosion (World of Darkness Rulebook, p. 178).<br /> <br /> <b>Ending the Tilt: </b>The effects of this Tilt normally only last for a single turn. The character can end the Tilt during<br /> her own action by reflexively spending a point of Willpower to gather her wits, though she suffers a \u20133 modifier to any actions she takes that turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that story-wise, it's as closest to the Condition I was looking for the witch hunters. But it still not working, mechanically speaking. There are three things in this that makes it not usable for hunters:<br /> <br /> 1. It works for one turn only. It maybe okay effect for taking beat from the baseball bat. It's not okay if you are fighting with reality wraping humans. The <i>most important</i> part of witch hunting is not to let the witch to cast spells. So it should be rather Condition with scene duration than messured in turns.<br /> <br /> 2. Ending with Willpower point is to low price. In this, mages would easily end the Condition, especially, as they have higher Willpower level after they Awakening.<br /> <br /> 3. Only -3 modifier is not making they really problematic spellcasting action that it would make practically unsable by character. Freshly Awakened character have easily Dice Pool 4 ( from Gnosis 1 + Arcanum 3 ) and middle expirianced mages up too 7-8 ( Gnosis 3-4 + Arcanum 4-5 ). Hunters should have chance to make this Dice Pool lower than 3, because at least 3 dices is almost sure 1 success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-09-2015, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T14:11:44-07:00","id":509233,"title":"","content":"I can appreciate what you are trying, but humans are the cannon fodder of the nWoD. I might let a special NPC hunter have something like shield breaker, but having it as a standard template is a bit much. A human, even a trained one, should not be able to kill a mage easily. If they want to hunt the Awakened, they need to find other tactics. Invisible knock-out gas would be a good starter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2060-cthulusbuttcheeks","name":"CthulusButtCheeks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T14:20:02-07:00","id":509237,"title":"","content":"Simply put, you aren't going to get any straight up, you are unable to cast mechanics barring things like keeping them unconscious. Even keeping them drugged is only going to apply heavy penalties since it's still possible to form an imago, albeit a sloppy one. Which means you're going to have to continually reapply whatever Condition/Tilt you're using that keeps them out of it, whether that be by knocking them out every time they regain consciousness, or keeping them constantly drugged with an IV drip or something.<br /> <br /> Simply put, there is not and should not be an easy way to do this. If they want to hold a mage captive they're simply going to have to deal with the fact that this is really hard and a lot of work, and know that any slip up can end in disaster for them. You can't really wholesale stop a supernatural from accessing their powers, the best you can do really is try to keep them in a state where they're unable to attempt to use them.<br /> <br /> Also, considering that a starting mages base spellcasting dicepool in a single turn is a 7 at best (3 arcana + 3 gnosis + 1 yantra), a -3 penalty without the ability to add +3 from willpower is pretty significant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 05-09-2015, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T16:50:47-07:00","id":509306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CthulusButtCheeks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=509233#post509233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can appreciate what you are trying, but humans are the cannon fodder of the nWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the times you are right - but we talk here about Conspiracy-level Hunters, having they own &quot;powers&quot; or &quot;power items&quot;. If thinking about <i>Malleus Maleficarum</i> senior member, good comparison is Father Anderson from <b>Hellsing</b>. Let the video be best inspiration... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_nz_QRkwyQ0\" data-code=\"_nz_QRkwyQ0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/_nz_QRkwyQ0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> He is not in near the capabilities of Banisher, but clearly, his prayers are supernatural in nature. And he loves to use his double knives. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And others Conspiracy-level senior Hunters are on pair with Father Anderson, whatever if they are <i>Malleus</i>, <i>Task Force: Valkyrie</i> or from <i>Aegis Kai Duro</i> - they all have their own &quot;toys&quot; that even the odds against the monsters. Basically, they all are Minor Templates, like psychics or mystics from <b>Second Sight</b>. <b><i>Plus</i></b> the training of their own Conspiracy. I say they should be really good on fighting low to middle experienced Awakened, at least on cell ( players group ) level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CthulusButtCheeks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=509233#post509233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might let a special NPC hunter have something like shield breaker, but having it as a standard template is a bit much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shield Breaker is Endowment - you must be member of the Conspiracy, rather high-ranked, to get to use it. Dots in Merit need to be maximum of your Conspiracy Status. I say it's rather difficult to get high on Inquisition\u2019s world-wide ranking higher than Status 2. So by the rules, your typical <i>Malleus Malleficarum</i> member would take 2 points from Armor or Defense from Mage Shield. Senior Inquisitors maybe 3-4 points. <b>IF</b> touching themselves the targeted mage.<br /> <br /> The same goes to the <b>Sympathy Dummy</b> - those <b>powers</b> are to make Hunters a bit more like the monsters they hunt. It's even the <b><i>point</i></b> of Conspiracy level game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CthulusButtCheeks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=509233#post509233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A human, even a trained one, should not be able to kill a mage easily. If they want to hunt the Awakened, they need to find other tactics. Invisible knock-out gas would be a good starter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not always hunters want to kill Enemy. <i>Malleus</i>, for example, strive to capture witches, get their confession and try to &quot;convert&quot; them. It does not mean they will kill it outright. Hell, it's even my <b>Mage</b> session basic idea.<br /> <br /> Even if we go with killing scenario - I will highly disagree with &quot;ow, Hunters can stun mages when using highly specialized weapons or traps&quot; as real threat. Believe me, I saw what cabal of mages can go, only few weeks after their Awakening.<br /> <br /> Also, there are info in the gameline that Supernal Magic is <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ThoughtControlledPower\" target=\"_blank\">Thought Controlled Powers</a>. Without focused thought you cannot cast spells effectively or control you magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T17:19:09-07:00","id":509311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=509237#post509237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply put, you aren't going to get any straight up, you are unable to cast mechanics barring things like keeping them unconscious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all the time unconscious. But for the few minutes, up to one hour - enought to steal them to other location.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=509237#post509237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even keeping them drugged is only going to apply heavy penalties since it's still possible to form an imago, albeit a sloppy one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did we get rules that mages can cast spell if they had problem with Imago forming. At least as I remeber <b>Tome of Mysteries</b>, it made spell very <b>difficult</b> to cast. &quot;Bad Imago&quot; is main answer to the Failure on normal spellcasting roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tome of Mysteries</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cCreating the Imago\u201d is a fancy way to say that the mage visualizes the spell\u2019s effects. There is more to this, though, than simply imagining what she wants to happen. The mage must visualize the process from start to \ufb01nish.<br /> If she wishes to cast Forces 2 \u201cIn\ufb02uence Electricity\u201d to cause electricity to arc out from a wall socket and shock an enemy, for instance, she needs to start by focusing on her control over the Arcanum of Forces and how that control translates to changing the path of the energy running through the wires in the wall. She needs to picture that energy changing course, forcing its way out of the socket, traveling in a predetermined arc and striking her enemy.<br /> A waver in Imago can cause disastrous results \u2014 the spell might mis\ufb01re and hit the wrong person, or it<br /> might simply deliver a painful shock to the next person to use the socket but not have any immediate effect. Add to this the fact the mage might have only a few seconds (that is, one turn) to create the spell, and it\u2019s easy to see why even \u201csimple\u201d spells can be exhausting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I now see the blunty penalty to spellcasting roll is bad thing to go with it. More logical, is that Awakened character need to roll each time his Paradox Dice Pool, as his magic is spliping him away with Unfocused Condition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=509237#post509237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which means you're going to have to continually reapply whatever Condition/Tilt you're using that keeps them out of it, whether that be by knocking them out every time they regain consciousness, or keeping them constantly drugged with an IV drip or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it was idea from the begining. I just point out Unfocused should be Condition, not Tilt, as Tilt is resolved in matter of seconds ( one-two turns ). The druge dosage need for the Unfocuse, or shock needed to be putted on mage would last at least few minutes. And character should be able to make action to beat this - i.e. resolve the Condition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=509237#post509237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply put, there is not and should not be an easy way to do this. If they want to hold a mage captive they're simply going to have to deal with the fact that this is really hard and a lot of work, and know that any slip up can end in disaster for them. You can't really wholesale stop a supernatural from accessing their powers, the best you can do really is try to keep them in a state where they're unable to attempt to use them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was also the part of the plan from begining. Witch Hunters need to be able to drug and take the characters out to transport and probably lock them ( inside nice Thaumium filled cell ). The bit problem is when Hunters want to do <b>other</b> things than killing the character - like <i>Malleus </i>wants, most of the time, the &quot;confession&quot; of witch and let her give last time to convert and repent for her sins. When Tortured, Awakened charcter should be enough concies to be able to speak and make half-reasonable desicions - but not enought to reliably use magic. And here comes second time the Unfocused Condition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=509237#post509237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, considering that a starting mages base spellcasting dicepool in a single turn is a 7 at best (3 arcana + 3 gnosis + 1 yantra), a -3 penalty without the ability to add +3 from willpower is pretty significant.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still a 4 dices to the roll - almost sure sucess to get. Expirianced mages would not hae any problems with getting more succeses. But reading <b>Tome of Mysteries</b>, I see the problem was not the Dice Pool - real problem is that spell works, only the Imago was badly created. And this is nearly definition of Paradox. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-09-2015, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T21:14:24-07:00","id":509561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=509311#post509311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was also the part of the plan from begining. Witch Hunters need to be able to drug and take the characters out to transport and probably lock them ( inside nice Thaumium filled cell ). The bit problem is when Hunters want to do <b>other</b> things than killing the character - like <i>Malleus </i>wants, most of the time, the &quot;confession&quot; of witch and let her give last time to convert and repent for her sins. When Tortured, Awakened charcter should be enough concies to be able to speak and make half-reasonable desicions - but not enought to reliably use magic. And here comes second time the Unfocused Condition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is there isn't really a state you can put a mage in (that I can reasonably justify anyway) to where they are able to make half-reasonable decisions yet are unable to cast (this is assuming no archmaster shenanigans and the like). If they possess enough clarity of mind to even be able to make <i>unreasonable</i> decisions they have enough mental clarity to cast magic.<br /> <br /> If they're drugged up they'd be hard pressed to cast, sure, but they'd still be able to. If they were drugged up hard enough to where they can't then chances are they aren't in a state where they're going to be deciding anything for anyone. Honestly, trying to hold them in a state where they have no conscious control over their magic seems like a good way to create one of the Mad, and that isn't going to end well for anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T22:27:02-07:00","id":509586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=509561#post509561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is there isn't really a state you can put a mage in (that I can reasonably justify anyway) to where they are able to make half-reasonable decisions yet are unable to cast (this is assuming no archmaster shenanigans and the like). If they possess enough clarity of mind to even be able to make <i>unreasonable</i> decisions they have enough mental clarity to cast magic.<br /> <br /> If they're drugged up they'd be hard pressed to cast, sure, but they'd still be able to. If they were drugged up hard enough to where they can't then chances are they aren't in a state where they're going to be deciding anything for anyone. Honestly, trying to hold them in a state where they have no conscious control over their magic seems like a good way to create one of the Mad, and that isn't going to end well for anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just imagine a Mage with Life 4 and Forces 4 tripping balls: &quot;Holy shit, everyone is <i>colors</i>, this is incredible!&quot; Except the Hunters, instead of going &quot;lol, this mage is fucked <i>up</i>&quot; are now, in fact, shimmering pillars of multicolored light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T22:44:23-07:00","id":509594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=509561#post509561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, trying to hold them in a state where they have no conscious control over their magic seems like a good way to create one of the Mad, and that isn't going to end well for anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>We talk about Hunters here, men. Even their &quot;mercy&quot; is only as long, as you stick to their terms - and in reality, work for them to repent for your &quot;mistakes&quot;. <b>Hunter</b> books mentions that <i>Long Night</i> ( protestant &quot;born again&quot; christian cult Hunters ) may let witch to work for them. But most <i>Malleus</i> is going to take &quot;confession&quot; and end witches misery. Other groups are a likely diversed in their view - <i>Task Force: Valkyrie</i> may employ wizard, if you sever most of ties with your old life. Where <i>Null Mysteriies</i> could take you for months as lab rat. And many others takes on &quot;Thou shalt not suffer a witch to live&quot; exist in Hunters world. Majority still end in your death, one way or another.<br /> <br /> Most of time, you do not need to worry about witch becoming the Mad - it's quite simple thing - they kill it or let it live, knowing it <b>before</b> they hunt the witch. And even if Awakened would gone Mad because of witch hunters practice - I'm really okay with that implication. I even think it's rather cool and logical idea - wronged witch is force to be rekon. That's why you will try to kill it. And even there, those things can happen... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7xo9itaw4Is\" data-code=\"7xo9itaw4Is\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/7xo9itaw4Is/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-10-2015, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T22:48:32-07:00","id":509596,"title":"","content":"But at that point they'd be dealing with a mage whose magic was out of control. Sure, they may have jumped the mage and captured them the first time, but now they have a guy sitting in their base turning everything that comes within 20 yards of him into pretty multicolored lights with no way to turn it off. That is <i>not</i> a good thing for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T23:34:00-07:00","id":509645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=509586#post509586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just imagine a Mage with Life 4 and Forces 4 tripping balls: &quot;Holy shit, everyone is <i>colors</i>, this is incredible!&quot; Except the Hunters, instead of going &quot;lol, this mage is fucked <i>up</i>&quot; are now, in fact, shimmering pillars of multicolored light.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I think it's very cool antagonistic crossover idea here - locking mages long term is dangerous, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=509596#post509596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But at that point they'd be dealing with a mage whose magic was out of control. Sure, they may have jumped the mage and captured them the first time, but now they have a guy sitting in their base turning everything that comes within 20 yards of him into pretty multicolored lights with no way to turn it off. That is <i>not</i> a good thing for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say the thing you describe is very natural implication of prisoning and torturing Awakened by some longer period of time. Key word here is <i><b>longer</b></i>.<br /> <br /> I do not think that torturing mage by mearly few hours to get &quot;confessions&quot; or to get informations your witch hunters need is problem of Awakened soul to split up and every Hunter in vicinity becoming unreal fragments of his Supernal imagination. Wizard will be pissed as hell if he will live this encounter, but this kind of psychological or biochemistry break downs are parts of everyday Sleepers lives - even if very rare. You can have large drug poisoning. Or your family member is dead and you take this <i>really</i> hard - you cannot think straight. Most of time, you need just couple of days to return to sense of self. And then you move on.<br /> <br /> I would envision general rule for stuations something like this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For each day the mage is left with Unfocused Condition or is tortured, he lose one point of Wisdom. This means that character can become Mad. If she is freed from her suffering before this, she returns to her previous Wisdom level by one point per day. </div> </div> </div>And yes, this can easily lead to the much larger threat than Witch Hunters caught in the first place. It's Hunters call to let free the mage or end it quickly. &quot;Thou shalt not suffer a witch to live&quot; was coinsidance not without reason...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T00:07:20-07:00","id":509687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=509645#post509645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not think that torturing mage by mearly few hours to get &quot;confessions&quot; or to get informations your witch hunters need is problem of Awakened soul to split up and every Hunter in vicinity becoming unreal fragments of his Supernal imagination. Wizard will be pissed as hell if he will live this encounter, but this kind of psychological or biochemistry break downs are parts of everyday Sleepers lives - even if very rare. You can have large drug poisoning. Or your family member is dead and you take this <i>really</i> hard - you cannot think straight. Most of time, you need just couple of days to return to sense of self. And then you move on.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they'd be getting spells cast at them long before they ever got any sort of confession, which is my point. You aren't really going to be able to have them in a state to confess anything without them also being in a state where they can use magic. You also can't really turn off their magic, because that's one of those things that require archmaster levels of ability. So you can either just kill them, keep them locked in a state where they can't function at all, or deal with a pissed off (if high as a kite) mage casting awakened magic every which way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T04:48:49-07:00","id":509783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=509687#post509687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they'd be getting spells cast at them long before they ever got any sort of confession, which is my point. You aren't really going to be able to have them in a state to confess anything without them also being in a state where they can use magic. You also can't really turn off their magic, because that's one of those things that require archmaster levels of ability. So you can either just kill them, keep them locked in a state where they can't function at all, or deal with a pissed off (if high as a kite) mage casting awakened magic every which way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point taken - I will investigate more c<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/509787-malleus-maleficarum-and-monster-s-confessions\">onfession taking of <i>Malleus</i> on <b>Hunter</b> forum</a>. Also - should not Hunter cell being treated as few witnesses for the Vulgar spells, in context of Paradox?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">In the meantime </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">- there is also another way for the Witch Hunters to make problems with spell casting for Awakened characters without making them unconsciousness. In <b>Second Sight</b> there was Merit called </span><i>Doubting Thomas</i><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">, that made using powers in character's vicinity more difficult. Should not Witch Hunters have thing like this for the Paradoxes?</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-10-2015, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T05:34:31-07:00","id":509810,"title":"","content":"Besides, loads of Mages have loads of ways to be able to purge their system of intoxicants, or to twist their senses and mind to resist them/act normally regardless.<br /> <br /> How dangerous any Mage is relies considerably more upon the Mage than upon Mages in general. Unlike Vampires and Werewolves, two Mages may have no supernatural abilities in common at all, though each will be exceptionally dangerous in their own way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T06:22:07-07:00","id":509816,"title":"","content":"I would say that all the preparations Hunters make will fall apart if the mage in question cleverly applies some contingency spells with optional Fate 2 into his pattern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T09:25:57-07:00","id":510767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=509810#post509810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How dangerous any Mage is relies considerably more upon the Mage than upon Mages in general. Unlike Vampires and Werewolves, two Mages may have no supernatural abilities in common at all, though each will be exceptionally dangerous in their own way.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I disagree with your second point (a vampire with Majesty/Dominate maxed is quite different from one with Protean/Vigor), the first is immensely true.<br /> <br /> I've got a Moros in one of my games at the moment who, despite being a Gnosis 6 legend in his local community (he is a knight-artificer type, who has built some truly mythic objects), only just bought Space 2. What most Mages consider a necessity, he's never bothered with. He has no capacity to read the future or scry. Instead, he relies on mere invulnerability; being so armoured as to make assault a pointless endeavour.<br /> <br /> Understandably, fellow Mages consider him sort of a dupe who, while heroic and impressive and not someone to cross, is still leaving himself massively vulnerable.<br /> <br /> But for a Hunter, he represents a considerably different kind of enemy than his Acanthus cabal-mate, who can see the future with astonishing precision and who is second to none at tracking living things, yet who has relatively few defenses against non-magical assault.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the kinds of paranoia Mages specialize in is most frequently paranoia against their own. It wouldn't surprise me if many of them were astonishingly vulnerable to mundane assault. That goes double if the Hunter who's the least bit savvy. An Acanthus who regularly prophecies &quot;Will someone attack me this week?&quot; might not think enough of the Hunter to consider that he might be a decoy while his friends plant a bomb in the Mage's car.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T09:47:25-07:00","id":510819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=510767#post510767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I disagree with your second point (a vampire with Majesty/Dominate maxed is quite different from one with Protean/Vigor), the first is immensely true.<br /> <br /> I've got a Moros in one of my games at the moment who, despite being a Gnosis 6 legend in his local community (he is a knight-artificer type, who has built some truly mythic objects), only just bought Space 2. What most Mages consider a necessity, he's never bothered with. He has no capacity to read the future or scry. Instead, he relies on mere invulnerability; being so armoured as to make assault a pointless endeavour.<br /> <br /> Understandably, fellow Mages consider him sort of a dupe who, while heroic and impressive and not someone to cross, is still leaving himself massively vulnerable.<br /> <br /> But for a Hunter, he represents a considerably different kind of enemy than his Acanthus cabal-mate, who can see the future with astonishing precision and who is second to none at tracking living things, yet who has relatively few defenses against non-magical assault.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the kinds of paranoia Mages specialize in is most frequently paranoia against their own. It wouldn't surprise me if many of them were astonishingly vulnerable to mundane assault. That goes double if the Hunter who's the least bit savvy. An Acanthus who regularly prophecies &quot;Will someone attack me this week?&quot; might not think enough of the Hunter to consider that he might be a decoy while his friends plant a bomb in the Mage's car.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The primary point I derived from your comment is one of the great fundamentals of mage society - cabals are very important for safety and security, both against other mages and mortals. While your Moros might be vulnerable to magical assault or surprise, and the Acanthus lacks protection against more mundane violence, <i>together</i> they are not particularly vulnerable at all, and that's before any other cabal-mates are factored into the equation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T11:24:26-07:00","id":510928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=510767#post510767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I disagree with your second point (a vampire with Majesty/Dominate maxed is quite different from one with Protean/Vigor), the first is immensely true.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that ability wise, this is correct. But the approach a Hunter will take is going to be similar. Assuming they know what they are hunting:<br /> <br /> For Vampires: Daylight, Fire, Stakes,Object to remove a head (ok, this kills nearly everyone, but still).<br /> For Werewolves: Silver bullets. Silver knives. Grenades with Silver Shrapnel. Did I mention Silver?<br /> For Changelings: All the lore discusses this &quot;cold iron&quot; thing...<br /> For Prometheans: Torches and Pitchforks (w/o the pitchforks), flamethrowers.<br /> For Spirits/Ghosts: Find bans, find Banes, destroy fetters, exorcise<br /> <br /> Mages are weird. Theoretically, you can kill them just like any normal human, even though they can shoot lightning and stop time. But sometimes you can't. Some might have magic/attainments that allow them to heal ridiculously fast. Some might have armor/damage resistance that makes tanks blush. Some can flash step out of the way of any harm. And those are just <i>some</i> of them.<br /> <br /> That is what makes mages so frustrating to hunt. Short of paradox, their are few limits that exist for what a mage might be able to do. So it is hard to prepare for mages beyond confronting them with lots of sleepers (which raises the whole issue of bystanders), since you don't know what they can do.<br /> <br /> (The only other gamelines I know of that can be similar are Mummyand Geist. Mummies are forces of nature, and hunting them just seems...a bad idea. Geists have their mementos, which if destroyed do weaken them, but that is assuming you can get your hands on one. I would throw demons on this list, but I can't remember if they have any weaknesses/supernatural resistances.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","user":"Freemind","date":". 05-11-2015, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2813-freemind","name":"Freemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1333"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T14:15:31-07:00","id":511118,"title":"","content":"I made new Endowment to talk about and making restraining witches possible. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Magic Warding</b><br /> <br /> When Hunters get the witch in the confinement of the Safehouse, they need to make sure he will not leave it. Or that magic from the outside will interfere with they safety. This Endowment make sure that spells will be outside of area or locked inside. When used on item touching the witch, it can even close her magic within. Using this Endowment needs marking the warded territory or item with symbols of some kind \u2013 destroying the markings, ends the effect immediately.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Extended; each roll represents one minute of marking area or item with symbols. The Endowment may be \u201crushed,\u201d reducing the time per roll to one turn at the cost of incurring a -1 penalty on the roll. If used on the area, hunter must roll a number of successes equal to the number of square yards the blessing\u2019s protection encompasses. If using it on the item he must accumulate items Size in successes,<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Resolve + Endowment Merit<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: </b>Warded area or item empower magic, not diminish it. Every power used on the target of Endowment gets Endowments Merit bonus to the spellcasting rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure: </b>No progress is made toward warding the area.<br /> <br /> <b>Success: </b>The character makes progress toward warding the area or item from magic.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>Penalty to active magic in area or by the character touching item is three times Endowment Merit.<br /> \u200b<br /> At successful usage of Endowment, warded area or item touching witch gives her penalty equal twice the Endowment Merit to all spellcasting and magic activation rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Suggested Modi\ufb01ers</b><br /> +2 Item or area are connected to the idea of restrain \u2013 like shackles, prison cell or chain.<br /> <br /> <b>Variants Example:</b> Consecrate shackles marked with cross on inside ( Benedictions )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-11-2015, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T06:37:46-08:00","id":820306,"title":"","content":"Watched today great film on topic - <b>Last Witch Hunter</b> with Vin Diesel - and it's greatly show complex relations between <b>Hunter</b> Conspiracies and <b>Mage</b> Consilium. It's really interesting how <i>Malleus Maleficarum</i> ( as <a href=\"http://www.axeandcross.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Axe and Cross</i></a> in movie ) can police, but also be clearly antagonistic to witches - I'm stealing whole idea to my games. Seeing how plot unfold in my play, I can clearly see the MM coming to some Consilia that do not grip their problems together and say &quot;If you do not solve it yourself, <b>we</b> will come and resole this - with you on stakes&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ky4sXEz520Y\" data-code=\"Ky4sXEz520Y\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Ky4sXEz520Y/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <b>As to technical matter how Witch Hunters hunt the witches?</b> They use magic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, there are few really interesting mages concepts in movie. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T09:42:38-08:00","id":820388,"title":"","content":"Going to a bunch of mages and telling them to do something or else is literally one of the worst things any Hunter of any stripe can possibly do. You've let them know ahead of time that they have another problem to deal with and likely tipped your hand to the nature of that problem. That is suicide.<br /> <br /> And as for Witch Hunters hunting witches using magic, yes, those are called Banishers. And yes, they can pose a bit of a problem. Probably not for very long if they come out and politely introduce themselves, they'd be dead within the hour, but a problem nonetheless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T10:49:59-08:00","id":820436,"title":"","content":"Technically, he used alchemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T11:15:09-08:00","id":820450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=820388#post820388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going to a bunch of mages and telling them to do something or else is literally one of the worst things any Hunter of any stripe can possibly do. You've let them know ahead of time that they have another problem to deal with and likely tipped your hand to the nature of that problem. That is suicide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternative is the Vatican hit squads coming over to &quot;resolve the issue&quot; with Left Handed mages - as both sides protect the Veil and Sleepers lives - I can see Conspiracies as making a pressure on the Consilium.<br /> <br /> Or as how my London's Adamant Sage say it: &quot;We let them kill one or two a year some crazy Scelasti and they give us more or less free hand to take care of our kind. Both sides do not - <i>really </i>- want open war.&quot;<br /> <br /> Because, in the other way, all sides loose...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LLVKxm3_Qwg\" data-code=\"LLVKxm3_Qwg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/LLVKxm3_Qwg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-01-2016, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T11:23:20-08:00","id":820453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=820450#post820450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alternative is the Vatican hit squades coming over to &quot;resolve the issue&quot; with Left Handed mages - as both sides protect the Veil and Sleepers lives - I can see Conspiracies as making a pressure on the Consilium.<br /> <br /> Or as how my London's Adamant Sage say it: &quot;We let them kill one or two a year some crazy Scelasti and they give us more or less free hand to take care of our kind. Both sides do not - really - want open war.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that most Consilia are in open talk with Hunters. Long story short, they don't really need anyone else's permission to take care of their own. If they're going to take care of their own, they will. If they aren't, they wont. If some sort of Sleeper organization tries to butt in and tell them how to run things they'll likely be dealt with. And if someone tries to send hit squads, they're probably gonna have a bad time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T11:31:06-08:00","id":820460,"title":"","content":"It depends on what kind of power the Hunters are packing in the crossover. If they are a serious threat, they will be negotiated with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T11:51:00-08:00","id":820471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=820460#post820460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on what kind of power the Hunters are packing in the crossover. If they are a serious threat, they will be negotiated with.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would honestly more depend on the people in the consilium. To me this would fall under some sort of 'We do not negotiate with terrorists' policy, but some people would likely be perfectly fine with it. Location also plays a pretty big role. If this is some nowhere backwaters that only has a handful of mages then they might submit, but any large consilium would likely just say, lolnope, we do what we want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T11:59:32-08:00","id":820474,"title":"","content":"I think the idea is that, if the crossover settings are calibrated appropriately, the Hunters won't be seen as a rogue terrorist group but as a neighbouring country.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T12:04:17-08:00","id":820482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=820474#post820474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the idea is that, if the crossover settings are calibrated appropriately, the Hunters won't be seen as a rogue terrorist group but as a neighbouring country.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least on Conspiracy level - we do not talk here of few lone hunters against few dozen Concilium. We say, for example, Vaticans all holy crusaders against few dozen mages Concilium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-31-2016, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T13:03:42-08:00","id":820523,"title":"","content":"Doesn't much matter, Mage organizations are also greater than Hunter ones. They have the numbers, but that's their only advantage. You'd also be skirting the edge of the Torn Veil type of game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T13:18:56-08:00","id":820537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=820474#post820474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the idea is that, if the crossover settings are calibrated appropriately, the Hunters won't be seen as a rogue terrorist group but as a neighbouring country.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they walk into your territory, tell you to do what they want or else, I don't really expect them to be met as allies or as anything other than a rogue terrorist group. Now if they nicely offer to help you with your problems we're talking about a completely different situation, but going by the scenario presented I'm not thinking that's the case. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=820482#post820482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At least on Conspiracy level - we do not talk here or few lone hunters against few dozen Concilium. We say, for example, Vaticans all holy crusaders against few dozen mages Concilium.</div> </div> </div> </div>You said it yourself, no one wants to wage open war here. But that's what you're suggesting that the Vatican or whatever it is do. The mages are just doing what they always do, going about business as usual. You're saying that the Hunters or whoever barge in, tell them to do what they say or wage open war, which is something you have again pointed out they don't want. So if the mages say no, we're going to keep doing what we've been doing, it will be the opposing force who would have to start open conflicts, which for the third time, they don't want to do. <br /> <br /> And if they <i>do</i> start things using any sort of real force, you're likely going to have an Adamant Sage rallying the Arrow world wide, and likely dragging the rest of the Orders into the fight along with them until the threat to the Awakened population has been taken care of. Long story short, it is a bad idea that is likely to backfire spectacularly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T13:41:29-08:00","id":820544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=820537#post820537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they walk into your territory, tell you to do what they want or else, I don't really expect them to be met as allies or as anything other than a rogue terrorist group. Now if they nicely offer to help you with your problems we're talking about a completely different situation, but going by the scenario presented I'm not thinking that's the case.<br /> <br /> <br /> You said it yourself, no one wants to wage open war here. But that's what you're suggesting that the Vatican or whatever it is do. The mages are just doing what they always do, going about business as usual. You're saying that the Hunters or whoever barge in, tell them to do what they say or wage open war, which is something you have again pointed out they don't want. So if the mages say no, we're going to keep doing what we've been doing, it will be the opposing force who would have to start open conflicts, which for the third time, they don't want to do.<br /> <br /> And if they <i>do</i> start things using any sort of real force, you're likely going to have an Adamant Sage rallying the Arrow world wide, and likely dragging the rest of the Orders into the fight along with them until the threat to the Awakened population has been taken care of. Long story short, it is a bad idea that is likely to backfire spectacularly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why would the Vatican want open war with a city full of mages, no less risk a potential worldwide conflagration that would put crosshairs on every piece of Catholic property and parishioner.<br /> <br /> It's a one way ticket for the Church to be declared a terrorist organization. The quiescence will ensure virtually no one remembers any mage using magic, and people associated with the church would ultimately be caught in armed conflict.<br /> <br /> Moreover, the retaliation would be swift, brutal and unforgiving. It would range from razing thousands of churches across the city, country and world to intentional and coordinated exposure of the most sensitive Church secrets. News of the Vatican openly waring against any major supernatural faction would also risk other factions like vampires and werewolves joining mages to protect their own interests and with a confident assumption that they would be the next targets.<br /> <br /> Simply, the Vatican, with or without significant supernatural resources, would have far too much to lose and would never, and could never, back-up such threats even using every advantage found in Hunter.<br /> <br /> Hunting is a game played in the shadows, and any group who values their lives or that of anyone else would never issue ultimatums directly to a consilium full of mages. If they needed or wanted something, they would quietly and respectfully work through intermediaries and tactfully negotiate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 01-31-2016, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T14:08:09-08:00","id":820557,"title":"","content":"I believe that was Ashenrogue's point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T14:14:56-08:00","id":820560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=820557#post820557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that was Ashenrogue's point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was emphatically agreeing with him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T14:27:15-08:00","id":820564,"title":"","content":"I see. Your opening obfuscated that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T14:28:39-08:00","id":820565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=820564#post820564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. Your opening obfuscated that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was questioning the entire premise of why the Vatican of all things would ever even consider such a strategy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T15:04:59-08:00","id":820582,"title":"","content":"Yes, I see that now, but it really wasn't clear then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T20:31:29-08:00","id":820703,"title":"","content":"As currently written, mortals would have an extraordinarily difficult time overtly threatening Mages, even with some access to supernatural powers. <br /> <br /> Giving a Mage warning that you're going after them is a very foolhardy action, you're giving them time to prepare and deal with you often in ways that you can't even detect. If you threaten a Mage on Wednesday and get hit by a car in a random traffic accident on Thursday was it just bad luck or a Fate curse? If you fall sick on the Friday was it a Life spell or are you just catching that same cold the bishop had last week? If on the Saturday you wake up from a dream that made you see things a different way and forgive the Mages was it just an epiphany or did someone change your thoughts with Mind?<br /> <br /> Mortals can certainly harm Mages, but the absolute only way to do it is hard and fast, given them as little warning as possible and trying to catch them off guard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T01:20:43-08:00","id":1061477,"title":"","content":"On one latest Supernatural episodes was great idea of 'witch killing bullets' - it just remind me about my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/499949-art-of-witch-hunting-htv-perspective?p=508782#post508782\"><i>Mage Shield Breaker </i>Endowment</a>. Consecrate with this your bullets, bypass Awakened Mage Armor all together, and you have nice dead witches! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thinking more on the topic of 'witch killing bullets' - <b>There is no reason why Mage Armour bypassing Endowment cannot bypass also risen Defense.</b> If Werewolves can have ability to use Defense in firearms, Conspiracies can have Endowment that bypass Defense in the first place, in the firearms combat also. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b<br /> <br /> And I run with idea that any Conspiracy member with 'inner' Endowment on him, is treated as Sleepwalker in the first place - that means that fully initiated Knights of Saint George, Malleus Maleficarum and Lucifuge are all treated Sleepwalkers for Supernal Magic. Still, Conspiracy use <i>not fully</i> initiated members ( those without special Endowments ) as 'Sleepers Cannon Folder' - <b>best cell tactics is to have mixed party with high ranking 'Endowment casting' leader and few 'ground level' Sleeper hunters.</b> Automatic and rising Paradox in combat quickly make Awakened sweat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T03:55:54-07:00","id":1061499,"title":"","content":"About theme of the topic: there is no reliable mundane way to fight mages as a whole. Fighting the sole mage is possible, if you have extensive intel on him and you have an mundane edge on him. Fighting a cabal is almost always a suicide, because those don't have many weaknesses, usually paranoid enough to keep themselves safe from spying and usually have contingencies for the sudden attack, magical or mundane. Mages exist in the world, full of enemies and dangers - Seers, Banishers, Scelesti, hostile spirits, etc. Mundanes are the least of their worries, but most contingencies would work against them too. <br /> <br /> About spellcasting penalies: I think that every Condition and Tilt which makes it hard to concentrate and think straight can and should give spellcasting penalties. So pain, shock, lack of sleep, food and water, being drunk or drugged - all of those should give different spellcasting penalites. It's only fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T04:15:29-07:00","id":1061504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=1061499#post1061499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About spellcasting penalies: I think that every Condition and Tilt which makes it hard to concentrate and think straight can and should give spellcasting penalties. So pain, shock, lack of sleep, food and water, being drunk or drugged - all of those should give different spellcasting penalites.<b> It's only fair.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Magic isn't fair. I don't necessarily disagree that these things <i>might</i> cause penalties (though no more than they would to anyone else), but I really want to emphasize that <i>Magic isn't fair</i>. It's pretty much like using a bunch of cheat codes in a video game in which your opponent doesn't know how to. It gives a decisive advantage, and while skill still plays a part, the advantage is still almost always going to go to the one with Magic. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T04:42:28-07:00","id":1061506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=1061504#post1061504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magic isn't fair. I don't necessarily disagree that these things <i>might</i> cause penalties (though no more than they would to anyone else), but I really want to emphasize that <i>Magic isn't fair</i>. It's pretty much like using a bunch of cheat codes in a video game in which your opponent doesn't know how to. It gives a decisive advantage, and while skill still plays a part, the advantage is still almost always going to go to the one with Magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, replace word &quot;fair&quot; with &quot;logical&quot;. If magic is product of your thoughts (namely ability to imagine Imago), then everything that interferes with your ability to think is going to interfer with your ability to do magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T05:02:46-07:00","id":1061510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=1061506#post1061506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, replace word &quot;fair&quot; with &quot;logical&quot;. If magic is product of your thoughts (namely ability to imagine Imago), then everything that interferes with your ability to think is going to interfer with your ability to do magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, though generally any affliction dire enough to interfere with your casting will already either not let you act at all (Insensate, Stunned, etc.) or already applies a negative on just about everything, casting included (Wound Penalties).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T21:56:04-07:00","id":1061727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/499845-art-of-witch-hunting?p=1061477#post1061477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I run with idea that any Conspiracy member with 'inner' Endowment on him, is treated as Sleepwalker in the first place - that means that fully initiated Knights of Saint George, Malleus Maleficarum and Lucifuge are all treated Sleepwalkers for Supernal Magic. Still, Conspiracy use <i>not fully</i> initiated members ( those without special Endowments ) as 'Sleepers Cannon Folder' - <b>best cell tactics is to have mixed party with high ranking 'Endowment casting' leader and few 'ground level' Sleeper hunters.</b> Automatic and rising Paradox in combat quickly make Awakened sweat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking something like this, for some reason imagining a nun of some sort.<br /> <br /> You could easily justify some Deep Sleeper Merit that forced a +2 to Paradox, or based it off Gnosis the way Reach does rather than just the standard +1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-13-2017, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}